   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of sectors that are applying mechanisms and tools to support risk reduction, preparedness, recovery, and risk informed development.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The number of government sectors or administrative districts that have adopted and are actively using mechanisms or tools designed to integrate disaster risk considerations into their operations, planning processes, and service delivery. These mechanisms or tools may include risk assessments and hazard mapping, early warning and contingency plans, emergency preparedness and response plans, post-disaster needs assessments and recovery frameworks integration of DRM and Climate Change Adaptation in sectoral/district development plans, and application of building codes and land-use planning guidelines. Unit of measure: count of govt sectors/districts</narrative>
    </description>
