   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of communities supported with eco-DRR interventions</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">number of communities that have received technical, financial, or material support to implement Ecosystem-based Disaster Risk Reduction (Eco-DRR) interventions or mechanisms. Eco-DRR involves the sustainable management, conservation, and restoration of ecosystems to reduce disaster risks, enhance resilience, and provide co-benefits for biodiversity and livelihoods. Unit of Measure: count (number of communities) Disaggregation: by type of intervention (e.g., reforestation, wetland restoration),level of community engagement (passive beneficiaries vs. active implementers) and by hazard type addressed (e.g., flood, drought, erosion)</narrative>
    </description>
